This is the best approach I can think of.
Ansible will create a default rule for all hosts when a site-specific variable file is not provided.
If rules need to be applied based on site-specific thresholds, we will use site-specific variable files stored in the ansible/vars folder.
This approach allows Ansible to apply both default and site-specific rules in a clean and controlled way.

To create default rules, run:

ansible-playbook playbook.yaml


To apply site-specific rules using a variable file, run:

ansible-playbook playbook.yaml -e @site_specific.yaml


To override values inline (for example, host kcg1 with threshold=15%), run:

ansible-playbook playbook.yaml -e "node_config.host1.example.com.threshold=0.20"

